1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,443
大多数人担心自己的文字读起来像 AI 写的，
Most people are afraid that their writing sounds like AI,

2
00:00:03,443 --> 00:00:06,770
但他们其实并不知道这到底意味着什么，所以只能瞎猜。
but they don't actually know what that means, so they guess.

3
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:09,782
他们随便改几个句子，加个脏字。
They tweak random sentences. They throw in a swear word.

4
00:00:09,782 --> 00:00:12,730
删掉几个副词，盼着这样就能神奇地修好。
They cut a few adverbs and hope that that magically fixes it.

5
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:14,770
剧透警告：没用。
And spoiler alert, it doesn't.

6
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:20,170
在 2026 年，AI 文本里有一些非常具体的模式会反复出现。
In 2026, there are very specific patterns that show up in AI text over and over again.

7
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:22,930
而一旦你看见这些模式，就真的再也无法当作没看见了。
And once you see them, you really can't unsee them.

8
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:26,210
好消息是，只要你知道该找什么，这些问题是能修掉的。
The good news is if you know what to look for, they are fixable.

9
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:30,262
所以你可以保留 AI 的速度和力量，同时不让你的书读起来像那种
So you can keep the speed and power of AI without your book reading like a tourist

10
00:00:30,262 --> 00:00:33,710
念过研究生院的旅游手册。如果你是新来的，我叫 Jason。
brochure that went to grad school. Now, if you're new here, my name is Jason.

11
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:35,832
我已经用传统方式写了 14 本书，
I've written 14 books the traditional way,

12
00:00:35,832 --> 00:00:39,429
又花了三年在 Kindlepreneur 教作者如何写作和出版，
spent three years teaching authors at Kindlepreneur how to write and publish,

13
00:00:39,429 --> 00:00:42,458
现在我帮助写作者使用 AI，同时不丢掉自己的文风。
and now I help writers use AI without losing their voice.

14
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:45,230
我读过大量 AI 生成和 AI 辅助写作的文本。
I read a lot of AI-generated and AI-assisted writing.

15
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:48,942
在这个视频里，我想带你逐一拆解 7 个具体的错误
And in this video, I want to walk you through 7 specific mistakes

16
00:00:48,942 --> 00:00:50,350
这些错误会直接暴露出一件事：
that absolutely scream.

17
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:53,630
这是 AI 写的；更重要的是，每个错误该怎么修。
AI wrote this and more importantly, how to fix each one.

18
00:00:53,710 --> 00:00:56,436
我不会只丢下一句“写具体一点”就走人
And I'm not going to just say be more specific and move on

19
00:00:56,436 --> 00:01:00,229
因为我们要聊的是底层到底出了什么问题
because we're going to talk about what's actually going wrong under the hood

20
00:01:00,229 --> 00:01:03,594
以及你该怎么做。我们先从最大的那个开始。
and what you should do instead. Let's start with the big one.

21
00:01:03,594 --> 00:01:06,488
第一个错误是过度依赖比喻，
The first mistake is an overreliance on metaphors,

22
00:01:06,488 --> 00:01:08,311
尤其是那种
especially the kind of metaphors

23
00:01:08,311 --> 00:01:11,890
把强烈情感黏到模糊的无生命物体或概念上的比喻。
that glue big feelings onto vague inanimate objects or concepts.

24
00:01:12,330 --> 00:01:16,864
AI 很爱这种东西。你会看到城市在创新中呼吸，或者社区
AI loves this stuff. You'll see cities breathing with innovation or communities

25
00:01:16,864 --> 00:01:19,331
成为韧性与希望的织锦，
that are tapestries of resilience and hope,

26
00:01:19,331 --> 00:01:22,068
市场里充满机会带来的焦虑低鸣。
marketplaces with anxious hums of opportunity.

27
00:01:22,068 --> 00:01:26,274
每一句单独看也许有点诗意，但堆在一起，
And each line by itself might sound kind of poetic, but stacked together,

28
00:01:26,274 --> 00:01:29,277
它就不再像是一个人在挑选具体的比喻
it stops feeling like a human picking specific comparisons

29
00:01:29,277 --> 00:01:32,040
而像是一台卡在诗意模式里的机器。
and starts feeling like a machine stuck in poetry mode.

30
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,305
真正的写作者把比喻当作调味料，
Real writers use metaphors like seasoning

31
00:01:34,305 --> 00:01:36,760
不会把半瓶盐倒在食物上。
so you don't pour half a bottle of salt on your food.

32
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:39,589
你只是这里捏一点、那里撒一点，并且选择那些
You put a pinch here and there and you choose metaphors

33
00:01:39,589 --> 00:01:43,051
符合角色观点和具体情境的比喻。
that fit the character's point of view and the concrete situation.

34
00:01:43,051 --> 00:01:44,720
所以这里的修法很简单。
So the fix here is pretty simple.

35
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:47,032
删掉大部分比喻。如果你看到一页里
You cut most of them. If you look at a page

36
00:01:47,032 --> 00:01:49,809
每隔一句就是关于
and every second sentence is some grand image about the

37
00:01:49,809 --> 00:01:51,858
某样东西“心跳”的宏大意象，那就删减。
heartbeat of something, you trim that,

38
00:01:51,858 --> 00:01:56,017
只保留那一两个真正能揭示出具体内容的比喻，
keep the one or two metaphors that actually reveal something specific about the

39
00:01:56,017 --> 00:01:58,244
关于场景或角色的，其余全部删掉。
scene or character and then kill the rest.

40
00:01:58,244 --> 00:02:01,870
第二个错误是像学校作文一样过度解释含义。
The second mistake is over-explaining meaning, like a school essay.

41
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:06,542
AI 不喜欢相信你能自己领会，所以它会先给你一个不错的具体瞬间，
AI hates trusting you to get it, so it will give you a nice concrete moment

42
00:02:06,542 --> 00:02:10,638
然后立刻补上一句含糊的分析性句子，解释
and then immediately tack on a vague analytical sentence about what

43
00:02:10,638 --> 00:02:14,590
这个瞬间如何体现身份、记忆或人类处境。
that moment says about identity or memory or the human condition.

44
00:02:14,790 --> 00:02:17,492
或者它会用“总的来说”或“最终”来结束一个场景，
Or it will close a scene with overall or ultimately

45
00:02:17,492 --> 00:02:21,030
然后把你刚读到的所有内容的意义总结一遍。
and then summarize the significance of everything you just read.

46
00:02:21,190 --> 00:02:23,323
这跟学生写作时担心
That's exactly how students write when they're worried

47
00:02:23,323 --> 00:02:24,820
老师没抓到重点时一模一样。
that the teacher won't get their point.

48
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:28,620
而在创意写作里，这只会让你的故事读起来像一篇关于它自己的读书报告。
And in creative writing, it just makes your story feel like a book report about itself.

49
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:35,260
修法是用动作、画面或对白结束场景，而不是用评论。
The fix is to end scenes on action or images or lines of dialogue, not on commentary.

50
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:39,619
如果你发现自己不断拉远镜头，去谈这个在
If you find yourself constantly zooming out to talk about what this represents in

51
00:02:39,619 --> 00:02:43,540
抽象层面代表什么，那就把评论删掉，看场景是否依然成立。
abstract terms, you strip that commentary out and see if the scene still works.

52
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:47,300
90% 的情况下它依然成立。所以让读者自己去做一部分联想。
90% of the time, it does. So let the reader do some of the connecting.

53
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:50,610
这才让它像艺术，而不是像作业。
That's what makes it feel like art and not like homework.

54
00:02:50,730 --> 00:02:55,451
第三个错误是那种旅行指南式的吹嘘和宣传册语言。
The third mistake is this kind of travel-guide puffery and brochure language.

55
00:02:55,451 --> 00:02:58,598
这就是 AI 把每个地点都变成
This is where AI turns every location into something

56
00:02:58,598 --> 00:03:00,410
一个听起来像旅游网站的东西。
that sounds like a tourism website.

57
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:03,129
所以小镇总是坐落在某个地方的中心地带，
So towns are always nestled in the heart of something,

58
00:03:03,129 --> 00:03:06,230
街道总是文化与活动的繁华枢纽。
and streets are bustling hubs of culture and activity.

59
00:03:06,230 --> 00:03:10,680
咖啡馆可能会让游客一窥社区生活的丰富织锦。
Cafes might offer visitors a glimpse into the rich tapestry of community life.

60
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:13,732
没有地方只是那种闻起来像洒了啤酒的拥挤小酒吧。
Nothing is just a cramped bar that smells like spilled beer.

61
00:03:13,732 --> 00:03:17,440
每样东西都在展示些什么，又成为另一样东西的证明。
Everything showcases something and stands as a testament to something else.

62
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:21,422
在小说或回忆录里，这会彻底破坏代入感，因为真实的叙述者
In fiction or memoir, this completely breaks immersion because real narrators

63
00:03:21,422 --> 00:03:24,920
和真实角色不会像广告文案那样去描述自己的街区。
and real characters do not think about their own neighborhoods like ad copy.

64
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:28,622
改法是问自己：如果这个角色在向一个
The fix is to ask yourself, if this character were complaining about this place to a

65
00:03:28,622 --> 00:03:30,460
朋友抱怨这个地方，他们会怎么描述？
friend, how would they describe it?

66
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:33,583
这会剥掉宣传册式的语气，让你回到简单、
That strips away the brochure tone and you go back to a simple,

67
00:03:33,583 --> 00:03:36,749
落地的细节，比如闪烁的招牌、那张桌子、
grounded details such as the flickering sign, the table,

68
00:03:36,749 --> 00:03:39,980
还有那个总是早上 9 点就坐在那里喝金汤力的人。
the one guy who's always there at 9:00am with gin and tonic.

69
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:43,836
如果你的段落可以直接贴进旅游博客也毫无违和，
And if your paragraph could be pasted into a travel blog and still work,

70
00:03:43,836 --> 00:03:48,018
那它很可能太有 AI 味了。第四个错误是“同义词轮盘赌”，
it's probably too AI adjacent. The fourth mistake is synonym roulette,

71
00:03:48,018 --> 00:03:49,900
也叫“雅致换词”。
also called elegant variation.

72
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:53,125
人类会重复自己。我们会抓住某些词不放。
Humans repeat themselves. We latch on to certain words.

73
00:03:53,125 --> 00:03:54,980
一个角色把他的镇子叫“镇子”。
A character calls their town a town.

74
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:57,459
他们不会这一段叫它“定居点”，
They don't call it the settlement in one paragraph

75
00:03:57,459 --> 00:04:00,716
下一段叫“社区”，再下一段叫“城市中心”，
and then the community in the next and then the urban center after that,

76
00:04:00,716 --> 00:04:03,222
只为了避免重复。而 AI 恰恰相反，
just to avoid repetition. AI, on the other hand,

77
00:04:03,222 --> 00:04:05,290
特别执着于换词。
is obsessed with mixing up vocabulary.

78
00:04:05,490 --> 00:04:08,930
所以你会看到同一个事物被连续改名三四次。
So you'll see the same object renamed three or four times in a row.

79
00:04:09,210 --> 00:04:12,970
表面上很聪明，但实际会破坏作者的文风。
It feels clever on the surface, but what it actually does is destroy voice.

80
00:04:13,370 --> 00:04:16,296
读者不再觉得是某个具体的人在跟自己说话，
The reader stops feeling like a specific person is talking to them

81
00:04:16,296 --> 00:04:18,370
而会觉得像是一本同义词词典爆炸了。
and starts feeling like a thesaurus exploded.

82
00:04:18,610 --> 00:04:22,362
改法是允许自己重复那个最诚实的词。
The fix is to give yourself permission to repeat the honest word.

83
00:04:22,362 --> 00:04:24,724
如果你的 POV 角色是个 12 岁的孩子，
If your POV character is a 12-year-old kid,

84
00:04:24,724 --> 00:04:29,200
他们不会为了换花样而把学校叫成“教育机构”。
they are not going to call their school an educational institution just to spice it up.

85
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:32,200
你选出贴合文风的那个词，然后一直用它。
You pick the word that fits the voice and you keep that.

86
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:35,760
语言一致性是人类叙述者最大的标志之一。
Consistency of language is one of the biggest markers of a human narrator.

87
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,465
顺便说一句，如果你能坚持看到这里，
By the way, if you've made it this far,

88
00:04:37,465 --> 00:04:39,640
你可能会很适合 Story Hacker 会员。
you might be a good fit for the Story Hacker membership.

89
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,920
我会把链接放在下方，感兴趣可以了解更多。
I'll have a link down below so you can learn more about that if you are interested.

90
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:48,800
第五个错误是用假高级词回避简单的 is 和 are。
So the 5th mistake is dodging simple 'is' and 'are' with fake fancy words.

91
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:53,360
AI 对直接说“咖啡馆很小”或“市场很吵”有一种奇怪的害羞。
AI has this weird shyness about just saying the cafe is small or the market is loud.

92
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:58,588
相反，所有东西都在“充当”“成为”“标榜”“提供”“代表”。
Instead, everything serves as or stands as or boasts or features, offers, represents.

93
00:04:58,588 --> 00:05:00,770
房子不只是坐落在山上。
The house doesn't just sit on the hill.

94
00:05:00,850 --> 00:05:04,970
它“是坚韧的灯塔”。河流也不只是穿过小镇。
It stands as a beacon of resilience. And the river doesn't just run through the town.

95
00:05:05,370 --> 00:05:07,530
它“为日常生活提供了宁静的背景”。
It offers a serene backdrop to daily life.

96
00:05:07,850 --> 00:05:11,282
偶尔一两次没问题，但当每个名词都必须“充当”什么时，
One or two of those is fine, but when every noun has to serve as something,

97
00:05:11,282 --> 00:05:13,713
你的文章就开始像新闻稿了。
Your prose starts to sound like a press release.

98
00:05:13,713 --> 00:05:16,995
改法其实就是回到你的句子，问自己：
The fix is actually just going back to your sentences and asking,

99
00:05:16,995 --> 00:05:20,683
我能不能把这个动词换成简单的 is，而不丢失任何重要信息，
could I swap this verb for a simple is without losing anything important,

100
00:05:20,683 --> 00:05:24,250
这很有意思，因为过去给作者的建议正好相反。
which is funny because that used to be the opposite advice for authors.

101
00:05:24,410 --> 00:05:28,630
但现在因为 AI 往往做得太过，我们反而需要把它收回来。
But now because AI tends to overdo it, we now actually need to rein it back in.

102
00:05:28,830 --> 00:05:32,408
如果答案是能，就去试。你会惊讶地发现文字变得
If the answer is yes, try it. You'll be shocked at how much more grounded

103
00:05:32,408 --> 00:05:33,864
更扎实、更像人写的。
and human your writing feels

104
00:05:33,864 --> 00:05:35,907
只要你让简单的动词做它们该做的事，
when you simply let simple verbs do their job

105
00:05:35,907 --> 00:05:39,110
把花哨的动词留给真正需要提升的时刻。
and reserve the fancy ones for moments that actually need elevation.

106
00:05:39,350 --> 00:05:42,750
第六个错误是“不只是 X，而是 Y”句式。
The sixth mistake is the 'not just X, but Y.'

107
00:05:43,270 --> 00:05:46,990
也就是文本不停用排比结构来显得深刻。
This is where the text keeps leaning on parallel structures to sound deep.

108
00:05:46,990 --> 00:05:48,670
比如某样东西不只是一面镜子。
So something isn't just a mirror.

109
00:05:48,870 --> 00:05:51,830
它不是镜子，而是传送门。一个角色不只是在累。
It's not a mirror, but a portal. A character isn't just tired.

110
00:05:52,030 --> 00:05:53,687
他们不只是累，而是被折磨。
They're not just tired but haunted.

111
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:56,670
这个句式本身没有错，因为人类也会用。
This construction itself isn't evil because humans use it, too.

112
00:05:57,070 --> 00:06:00,346
问题在于，每当 AI 想显得深刻时就依赖它，
The problem is when AI leans on it every time it wants to sound insightful,

113
00:06:00,346 --> 00:06:04,111
它就像一根修辞拐杖。如果我说它不只是这个，还是那个，
it's like a rhetorical crutch. If I say it's not just this, it's also that,

114
00:06:04,111 --> 00:06:05,160
那它一定很深刻。
it must be profound.

115
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:07,498
读者很快就会识破这种模式，
Readers pick up on that pattern pretty fast,

116
00:06:07,498 --> 00:06:11,280
并开始觉得文本在费力地制造意义，而不是真正赢得意义。
and it starts to feel like the text is straining for meaning instead of earning it.

117
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:13,630
改法是把这个句式留给极少数、
The fix is to save that structure for rare,

118
00:06:13,630 --> 00:06:17,120
真正重要的时刻，其他时候就直接说那个东西是什么。
genuinely important moments and otherwise just say what the thing is.

119
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:19,860
你不必用巧妙的句法来表演深度。
You don't have to perform depth with clever syntax.

120
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:22,920
你可以通过场景中实际发生的事来展现深度。
You can just show depth by what actually happens in the scene.

121
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:26,617
第七个错误是机械化的“三段式排比”。
The seventh mistake is mechanical rule-of-three patterning.

122
00:06:26,617 --> 00:06:28,400
人类确实喜欢三件一组的列举。
Humans do like lists of threes.

123
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:31,807
这是一种自然节奏。但 AI 会把它拉满到极致，
It's a natural rhythm. But AI takes that and cranks it up to 11,

124
00:06:31,807 --> 00:06:36,345
于是整页里几乎每段描写都是“冰冷、安静、无情”，
so you get pages where almost every description is cold, quiet and unforgiving,

125
00:06:36,345 --> 00:06:41,136
或者“希望、记忆与韧性”，或者“经济上、社会上、文化上”。一开始，
or hope, memory and resilience, or economically, socially and culturally. At first,

126
00:06:41,136 --> 00:06:42,400
听起来还不错。
it sounds kind of nice.

127
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:45,489
接着你的耳朵就会开始注意到那种三段式排比的鼓点。
Then your ear starts to notice that three-part pattern drumbeat.

128
00:06:45,489 --> 00:06:48,480
它不再像个人文风，而开始像模板。
It stops feeling like a voice and starts feeling like a template.

129
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:52,600
改法是有意识地变化节奏。有些句子可以短促而直接。
And the fix is to vary your rhythm on purpose. Some sentences can be short and blunt.

130
00:06:52,930 --> 00:06:56,570
有些可以拉长。有些列两件事。有些列四件，有些一件不列。
Some can stretch. Some can have two things. Some can have four, some none.

131
00:06:56,770 --> 00:07:00,115
如果你大声读一页，注意到自己陷入那种像儿歌一样
And if you read a page aloud and you notice yourself falling into the sing-song

